{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466956-soaking-agg-in-breed-metis","id":1466956,"title":"Soaking AGG in Breed; Metis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-06T10:08:34-07:00","id":1466956,"title":"Soaking AGG in Breed; Metis","content":"Hi team,<br /> <br /> I'd like to get some clarification on the matter. The book states that soaking agg is not possible in breed form so would a Metis born Garou not be able to soak AGG in Crinos?<br /> <br /> A metis is born in his Crinos form, a form halfway between Homid and Lupus. An adult werewolf in Crinos is a killing machine, a massive, nine-foot tall monster plodding to battle on two stocky legs. The very sight of one conjures up images of an age long gone, when massive shapeshifters stalked the Earth and herded their flocks of human breeding stock.- W20 44<br /> <br /> Humans can\u2019t soak aggravated damage. Werewolves can soak aggravated damage with Stamina in any form except their breed form, with the exception of damage from silver.- W20 255<br /> <br /> Werewolves heal at an incredible pace. A Garou regenerates her worst bashing or lethal health level every turn. Homid- and lupus-breed Garou can regenerate a health level each day while in their natural forms if they are in critical condition, but doing so doesn\u2019t let them do much more than sleep. If they\u2019re conscious and moving around in their breed form, they heal as humans do. Metis are blessed with full regeneration in every form. - W20 256<br /> <br /> Is this to be taken as verbatim or can Metis soak AGG in Crinos but cannot soak silver in all forms?<br /> It just seems very off to me that a Crinos is able to dish out agg so easily with its natural weaponry but cant soak it just cause the said Garou was born in that form.<br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12544,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12544-diplo","user":"diplo","date":". 11-06-2021, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12544-diplo","name":"diplo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12544_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T11:12:18-07:00","id":1466963,"title":"","content":"Soaking in WtA is a bit needlessly complicated.<br /> <br /> I forget if W20 bothered to include this, but in Revised it was clarified that they do soak Agg in Crinos, but can never soak silver damage with just their Stamina like homids and lupups can in their breed forms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T23:59:40-07:00","id":1467017,"title":"","content":"So if one were to depend only on W20 (people do that..... saying &quot;revised isnt W20 and we play only W20&quot;) then would that mean they cant soak said agg damage in Crinos if born Metis?<br /> Or its just something that isnt clarified in W20 as compared to revised edition. I've always been playing it like you quoted but hey, I just wanted to get a general idea from the community as the final decision is always upto the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12544-diplo","name":"diplo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12544_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T02:40:15-08:00","id":1467032,"title":"","content":"I took a look again and W20 doesn't seems to make an exception to Metis not soaking Agg at Breed form (it does touch on the matter of Silver).<br /> <br /> So strictly speaking it just isn't there. It is clear in the sense that it's a clear rule and the exception just isn't there.<br /> <br /> But W20, especially the core, does have a number of problems with text not being properly copied from previous editions, so it <i>probably</i> isn't by design, and Revised is the go to for clarification on such situations.<br /> <br /> All I can say is that I find it weird for someone to be <b>that</b> stubborn in their interpretations of W20. The core book is a collection of information from all the other books, it's unavoidable that there are problems like those. Taking a too rigid interpretation on this particular matter serves no other purpose than be a dick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T10:35:13-08:00","id":1467070,"title":"","content":"Well, I haven't actually used the official soaking rules if I have a say in the matter for over 25 years now... I know a lot of people that are very easily swayed by, &quot;the rules are way too complicated to remember, create really weird edge cases, and don't really add anything worth remembering it all to play.&quot; Remembering what the books actually say is mostly for Internet discussions for me.<br /> <br /> But as much as I prefer W20 as an edition, I can't imagine using it without the Rev ST Handbook FAQ in mind regarding interpreting rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T11:45:31-08:00","id":1467081,"title":"","content":"The rules are undoubtedly excessively convoluted. Not that they don't make some sense, but they're just unnecessary, and show that the authors were too focused on <i>simulating</i>their vision of a Garou instead of giving them fun mechanics.<br /> <br /> It is always fun, though, to remember that fire is the Bane of Vampires... and everyone else as really everyone takes Agg from it. No weapon in RAW is more dangerous than a flamethrower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T12:17:26-08:00","id":1467087,"title":"","content":"Well, my simplified version that I think captures everything just fine:<br /> <br /> All Breeds soak bashing, lethal, and aggravated damage from most sources regardless of form. Homids and lupus can soak silver in their breed forms, but have reduced regeneration in their breed forms.<br /> <br /> Boom. Done. It's 95% the same as what the books say, without the 5% that throws everything off.<br /> <br /> The &quot;fire does Agg&quot; thing stems way back though, and even Vampire took on the idea that Agg is more than just supernatural damage, but also extremely grievous damage from mundane sources. Though flamethrowers aren't generally that good given how fire works in the WoD rules, and how easily most splats can just blow you up for trying to use one in a fight (combat flamethrowers aren't really a thing because every time people tried the systems prove too prone to killing the user and any allies standing near them; military flamethrowers are generally engineering tools). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T14:33:41-08:00","id":1467196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466956-soaking-agg-in-breed-metis?p=1467032#post1467032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I can say is that I find it weird for someone to be <b>that</b> stubborn in their interpretations of W20. The core book is a collection of information from all the other books, it's unavoidable that there are problems like those. Taking a too rigid interpretation on this particular matter serves no other purpose than be a dick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just that, whole sections of W20 are copy pasted verbatim from Revised!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T15:55:27-08:00","id":1467204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466956-soaking-agg-in-breed-metis?p=1467196#post1467196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just that, whole sections of W20 are copy pasted verbatim from Revised!</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that, and sometimes they literally just copied one piece of text and left another that was necessary, because it was a big undertake anyway. The book simply don't have room for every line.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it creates weird situations, like rules that changed, but have blocks of text referencing how they used to be. The chance of this bit on a Metis' soaking Agg being by design is very slim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T23:21:21-08:00","id":1467234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466956-soaking-agg-in-breed-metis?p=1467032#post1467032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core book is a collection of information from all the other books, it's unavoidable that there are problems like those. Taking a too rigid interpretation on this particular matter serves no other purpose than be a dick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I still believe that this is due to the fact that OPP was just founded and rushed W20 after the success of White Wolf's own V20.<br /> W20 did a lot of new stuff, like gifts, fetishes, rules on side stepping, lost cubs, and what not, but didn't really make an effort to consolidate and present a whole picture as a book.<br /> <br /> V20 did 2nd edition, and had sidebars on how revised changed the described status, for example. W20 was just copy and pasted from various sources, partly without correcting errors in the source material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T05:24:03-08:00","id":1467251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466956-soaking-agg-in-breed-metis?p=1467234#post1467234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I still believe that this is due to the fact that OPP was just founded and rushed W20 after the success of White Wolf's own V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 is exactly the same, it has zero to do with OPP being new. Almost the entire text of V20 is simply copy/paste, even the changes are made by just as little editing as possible.<br /> <br /> As an example, the rules for resisting/breaking Blood Bonds are unusable as RAW because they changed from the number of doses increasing diff to increasing successes needed, but in the line where they'll tell you the limit on this increase they re-use old text with un-matching rules.<br /> <br /> Werewolf may be a little worse, but in general the cause is just that the X20 core books were this kind of undertaking until then. They're gigantic books, whose main purpose is to cram as much mechanical content from an entire game line as possible, while receiving little adjust and a focus on improving the horrendous layout and content organization from previous cores. This's a lot of work outside the text compiling material, and makes for a confusing mess to tune the whole text no one in the team really wrote.<br /> <br /> From Mage onward what actually changes is the amount of original work on each book, and even then I'm not sure if it can be considered such a seamless job. But it does change the standard approach of the work to a more hands on that makes editing easier in general. Also, the fact that from Mage onward you have actually less crunch to delve into. Mage is far less rule-intensive outside the core in any edition, and other lines are simply smaller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T05:49:59-08:00","id":1467252,"title":"","content":"Well, I have no knowledge on actual hours that were invested into V20 and W20.<br /> I have used V20 to run a few games (while adopting multiple actions and Celerity from V20DA), and I didn't run into material that was completely new to me (having had not run a vampire game in 10 years or so). And V20, with mentioning of little sub-groups of clans and obscure disciplines and stuff like that, along with the &quot;this is 2nd Edition, this will happen in revised&quot;-sidebars felt a lot more like an Anniversary-Edition and tome compiling what was the height of the setting. W20 never gave me that feeling.<br /> That is not to say, that there aren't flaws in V20, like the one you describe. Which is sad.<br /> <br /> As I recall, OPP was new, when W20 was developed and it was clear, that it wouldn't be a One-Time-thing, but that there now was a license to make more X20-era books, with V20 Companion being on kickstarter and so on. So, what OPP set out to do with W20 might have been different from the beginning, consciously or subconsciously. When V20 was made the old WoD was still dead and what is now known as Chronicles of Darkness was the only WoD CCP's version of White Wolf made books for - V20 being the exception as a homage to the series that made the company. That alone changed the book, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Fans of 1st, 2nd and revised - era of the game didn't get a &quot;This is what the game was, up until now&quot;-Compilation book like V20. Which I find sad, because they might have deserved one.<br /> W20 and M20 are more like the 4th Edition, they are now considered to be.<br /> C20 and Wr20 on the other hand, feel more like such homages...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 11-09-2021, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T08:39:48-08:00","id":1467262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466956-soaking-agg-in-breed-metis?p=1467252#post1467252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20 and M20 are more like the 4th Edition, they are now considered to be.<br /> C20 and Wr20 on the other hand, feel more like such homages...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree here, and I'm actually glad that they're not such a thing.<br /> <br /> Outside the Original Trio, other lines were in general badly needing actual new editions, and at least C20 gave me that in spades, Wr20 I just started reading, so I don't know for sure, but I got the impression that it was the same in this regard.<br /> <br /> As someone who still had the old material fresh in mind for VtM and WtA, I admit I didn't read W20 so thoroughly, while V20 had the difference of being something I play far more frequently. But my own account only V20 was just and good an anniversary compilation, and W20 seemed to follow suit, or at least try. Both compile a lot of previous material, give too little updates to it as this wasn't their purpose, and have the good and bad of doing so.<br /> <br /> The inexperience of OPP at the time may have played a role in W20's final quality, as I said I didn't read it thoroughly enough to know, but the goal is a clear thing and the same as V20. Of course, that talking about core, since it was already evident that it wouldn't be just the core, indeed.<br /> <br /> But by M20 it was clear that treating X20 as a new edition was on the table and they tried. A lot of unique aspects of the game made Mage the best line of the three to try it out anyway. Different from the others, whose powers and Z-splats required a lot of individual mechanical attention, Mage is light in its specific rules, it's mostly the Magic system, so supplements never added as much to crunch, for example.<br /> <br /> You may say the result is a mixed bag. M20 have a lot of good decisions and new problems because of author's vision. But it did well enough to show that treating the X20 line as a new edition from core was indeed the way to go. And that's what Changeling and Wraith are, those lines desperately needed an actual new edition, and at least C20 I can say that deliver from core. And I never once using it (it is my current main chronicle) felt it let me down, even if I not always agree to some lore directions (in the amount to be expected at a new edition of any TTRPG).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T13:23:15-08:00","id":1467287,"title":"","content":"They could have made &quot;20th Anniversary&quot;-&quot;Best of&quot;-Books without new updated content or meta-plot-agnostic, and still created a 4th edition as a new edition, with more radical changes (but possibly not as radical as V5).<br /> <br /> Like I said, I can't tie it to specific things, it's just the feeling that W20 didn't deliver the feeling I got with V20, and C20 while browsing though it. For me W20 feels more like M20, with the clear idea, that it is the start of a re-vitalised oWoD, with multiple books and new stuff, not a one-off homage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 11-09-2021, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T14:32:58-08:00","id":1467293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466956-soaking-agg-in-breed-metis?p=1467287#post1467287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could have made &quot;20th Anniversary&quot;-&quot;Best of&quot;-Books without new updated content or meta-plot-agnostic, and still created a 4th edition as a new edition, with more radical changes (but possibly not as radical as V5).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually they couldn't. At the time they had the license for the X20, not for a new edition named as such. Also, X20 got traction, but doing a 4th edition wouldn't necessarily build on that traction, and given their financing method it wasn't simple to change projects that way. Doing everything through Kickstart does have its disadvantages.<br /> <br /> Still I can guarantee you: from C20 onward I definitely didn't see the proposal as just an homage and didn't wanted to. Anything less than a new edition would be a waste of effort. I love Changeling, but 2nd edition had just too many accumulated problems and no Revised of its own to solve them or even start to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}